=== PART 1: reconstruct the existing Figure-3 / rate_induced.py calculation ===
Exact ramp function z(t): z(t) = -1 + 2*smoothstep(t/T_ramp), smoothstep(r)=3r^2-2r^3, clipped to r in [0,1] (quasistatic.py:smoothstep). Forced open-loop via u_z chosen so z(t) tracks this EXACTLY regardless of the y-z coupling (quasistatic.slow_ramp_run).
Initial state: y(0)=-1, z(0)=-1, m(0)=v(-1)*(-1) [=mu*(-1,-1)], Sigma(0)=Omega(-1)^-1 [=Sigma*(-1), the endpoint-A equilibrium].
y is NOT held fixed: u_y=0 identically, so y evolves freely under y'=y-y^3+u_y=y-y^3 (coupled to z through mu*(y,z) inside the moment ODE, and through the u_z formula which subtracts (y-z) to force z's trajectory -- so y's free evolution DOES feed back into what u_z must be, but z(t) itself is still forced to the prescribed smoothstep exactly).
ODE integrated for Sigma(t): dSigma/dt = -(Omega(z(t))@Sigma + Sigma@Omega(z(t)) - 2I)/tau_x, tau_x=1 (dynamics.moment_rhs), via dynamics.integrate -> scipy.solve_ivp RK45.
Time interval simulated: EXACTLY [0, T_ramp] -- dyn.integrate(y0,z0,m0,Sigma0,T_ramp,...) in quasistatic.slow_ramp_run; there is NO post-ramp continuation in the original code.
Time interval over which max_t Lambda_3(t) was computed in the original right panel: EXACTLY [0, T_ramp] as well -- rate_induced.run_ramp() calls slow_ramp_run(T_ramp, n_eval) and takes res['L3'].max() over that SAME [0,T_ramp] array. CONFIRMED: the old maximum was computed ONLY during the ramp, never after it. (Answers audit Q1: YES.)
Number of output timepoints: n_eval=300 (rate_induced.run_ramp default) for the primary RAMP_DURATIONS set, n_eval=200 for the FINE_DURATIONS diagnostic sweep -- both far below this audit's 2000-point / refined-peak protocol.
ODE tolerances: dynamics.integrate defaults rtol=1e-9, atol=1e-11 (already tight; unchanged here for the reproduction step).
Candidate blankets: core5.enumerate_candidates() = all subsets of {4,5,6,7} (node 8 fixed external anchor, never a candidate), sizes 0..4; integrity.Lambda_K filters to |B|<=K.
Ties: Lambda_K's RETURNED VALUE is the exact minimum over the filtered candidates (not affected by tie tolerance); the tie tolerance (1e-6) only affects which B are reported as 'winners' alongside that exact minimum. The PLOTTED Lambda_3(t) curve is this exact minimum.
